#: build-src/install/post_install.md:1
msgid "Post installation"
msgstr ""

#: build-src/install/post_install.md:3
msgid ""
"Now you have an installed and working numahop instance. But the base "
"installation of numahop is rather empty. The first thing you must create "
"before anything else is the libraries declared inside the yaml configuration "
"files."
msgstr ""

#: build-src/install/post_install.md:7
msgid "Here is a list of things you might want to create:"
msgstr ""

#: build-src/install/post_install.md:8
msgid "User Groups and Users"
msgstr ""

#: build-src/install/post_install.md:9
msgid "Workflow Models"
msgstr ""

#: build-src/install/post_install.md:10
msgid "Contidion Report"
msgstr ""

#: build-src/install/post_install.md:11
msgid "Mail Templates"
msgstr ""

#: build-src/install/post_install.md:12
msgid "Export Configurations"
msgstr ""

#: build-src/install/post_install.md:13
msgid "Bibliographic Records mappings"
msgstr ""

#: build-src/install/post_install.md:14
msgid "Automatic Controls settings"
msgstr ""

#: build-src/install/post_install.md:16
msgid ""
"There is a default account with login `admin`. This account should only be "
"used to create new users and the administration tools."
msgstr ""

#: build-src/install/post_install.md:19
msgid "Adding a Library"
msgstr ""

#: build-src/install/post_install.md:21
msgid ""
"There should already be a library present with identifier `lib_library`. "
"This one can be used. If you want more or one with another identifer it "
"should be configured right after installation. Each library must be "
"referenced in the database and its identifier registered in the config file."
msgstr ""

#: build-src/install/post_install.md:26
msgid ""
"For each libraries declared create a library through the interface. Then you "
"need to edit the libraries inside the database to make the column "
"`identifier` match the names declared inside the yaml files. If the library "
"you created isn't defined in the yaml file you need to edit the yaml file "
"and add an identifer to it and restart numahop."
msgstr ""

#: build-src/install/post_install.md:33
msgid "-- Print all the libraries you declared through the interface.\n"
msgstr ""

#: build-src/install/post_install.md:34
msgid ""
"-- Modify the identifier \n"
"-- <lib-identifier> corresponds to the identifier set inside the yaml file.\n"
"-- <lib-name> corresponds to the name given to the library at the creation "
"in the web interface.\n"
msgstr ""

#: build-src/install/post_install.md:38 build-src/install/post_install.md:55
#: build-src/install/post_install.md:63
msgid "'<lib-identifier>'"
msgstr ""

#: build-src/install/post_install.md:38 build-src/install/post_install.md:50
#: build-src/install/post_install.md:55
msgid "'<lib-name>'"
msgstr ""

#: build-src/install/post_install.md:38
msgid ""
"-- Note it is ok to filter by the name as NumaHOP normally enforces it to be "
"unique. \n"
msgstr ""

#: build-src/install/post_install.md:41
msgid ""
"Once the libraries are created you can create the rest of the objects you "
"need for your use of NumaHOP."
msgstr ""

#: build-src/install/post_install.md:45
msgid ""
"If you have created other objects before the library column update by "
"accident here is how to fix it:"
msgstr ""

#: build-src/install/post_install.md:48
msgid ""
"-- Check and note what is the identifier generated by numahop by default.\n"
"-- <old-uuid> is what it is referenced as from now on.\n"
msgstr ""

#: build-src/install/post_install.md:51
msgid ""
"-- We need to disable the foreign key contraints checks while modifying the "
"libraries otherwise \n"
"-- the contraints will prevent the modification because other tables "
"reference this identifier.\n"
msgstr ""

#: build-src/install/post_install.md:57
msgid ""
"-- Print all tables corresponding to created objects that have a library "
"field and have rows.\n"
msgstr ""

#: build-src/install/post_install.md:60
msgid "'library'"
msgstr ""

#: build-src/install/post_install.md:60
msgid ""
"-- For each table corresponding to the created object fix the foreign key.\n"
"-- <old-uuid> is the value we \n"
msgstr ""

#: build-src/install/post_install.md:63
msgid "'<old-uuid>'"
msgstr ""

#: build-src/install/post_install.md:66
msgid "First user and user groups"
msgstr ""

#: build-src/install/post_install.md:68
msgid ""
"I advise you create a admin user profile with all rights allowed for each "
"libraries as the admin account configured in the yaml file can do some of "
"the things but there are a lot of functionality that are disallowed on this "
"account."
msgstr ""

#: build-src/install/post_install.md:73
msgid "You can also create user profiles that suits your needs."
msgstr ""

